│ loaded, extra_body fields may not be passed through or merged in   │
│ subsequent calls, which is why the openrouter provider extra_body  │
│ field is not supported in Aider.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The intended behavior is to extend this registration/loading       │
│ process so that:                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • The extra_body field from the model metadata files (if present) │
│    is recognized, preserved, and passed downstream.                │
│  • This allows Aider to forward extra_body parameters into the     │
│    kwargs of send_completion and ultimately to litellm. This       │
│    ensures that provider-specific parameters (like openrouter’s    │
│    order or transforms) declared in extra_body can be used         │
│    seamlessly.                                                     │
